{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NStatConjugateGeneral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NStatConjugateGeneral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Sort","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S5SO3FiberAction"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.nStat_eq_sumChoose2_conj_via_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.nStat_eq_sumChoose2_conj_via_general","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L267-L274","doc":"**`PartitionOf5.nStat_eq_sumChoose2_conj`, re-derived from the GENERAL (†)**\n(not `decide`).  Each `λ ⊢ 5` has decreasing parts, so the general identity\napplies; with the two bridges above it reproduces the corpus anchor,\nconfirming (†) subsumes the finite enum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.conjugate_parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.conjugate_parts","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L262-L265","doc":"The recursive `conjugate` equals the corpus hardcoded `PartitionOf5.conjParts`\nfor every `λ ⊢ 5` (a genuine transpose check). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.aStat_parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.aStat_parts","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L259-L260","doc":"`aStat` on a block's parts is the corpus `PartitionOf5.nStat` (same fold). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chiralityParity_eq_w0_sign_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chiralityParity_eq_w0_sign_general","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L240-L249","doc":"**UNCONDITIONAL general-`n` geometric chirality.**  For every partition, the\na-function-parity chirality `(-1)^{n(λ)}` equals the geometric\nlongest-element sign `(-1)^{Σ_i C(λ'_i,2)} = sgn(w₀^{S_{λ'}})` of the\nconjugate Young subgroup — the leg left conditional at `n ≤ 5` in\n`DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN`, now closed for all `n` by (†). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chiralityParity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chiralityParity","kind":"def","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L236-L238","doc":"Chirality parity `(-1)^{n(λ)}` (defeq to `deltaSignParity` in\n`DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.aStat_eq_sumChoose2_conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.aStat_eq_sumChoose2_conjugate","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L204-L226","doc":"**(†), general `n` (sorry-free).**  For any partition `λ` given by a\nweakly-decreasing list of parts, the a-function statistic equals the sum of\n`C(·,2)` over the conjugate partition's parts:\n\n    `aStat l = sumChoose2 (conjugate l)`.\n\nProof: induction on `l` (largest-row peeling).  Both sides drop by the same\nincrement `Σ (tail)` when the largest row is removed — `aStat` by\n`aStat_cons`, `sumChoose2 ∘ conjugate` by `sumChoose2_addRow_ge` (its\n`c.length ≤ a` hypothesis furnished by `length_conjugate_le` from\ndecreasingness) together with `sum_conjugate`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.length_conjugate_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.length_conjugate_le","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L188-L200","doc":"When `a` bounds every part of `l`, the conjugate's length (= the largest\npart) is `≤ a`.  Supplies the `c.length ≤ a` hypothesis of\n`sumChoose2_addRow_ge` at each peel of a decreasing partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sum_conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sum_conjugate","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L182-L186","doc":"The conjugate has the same number of cells: `Σ (conjugate l) = Σ l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sumChoose2_addRow_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sumChoose2_addRow_ge","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L154-L178","doc":"**The row-increment on `sumChoose2`.**  When the new row `a` is at least as\nwide as the current diagram (`c.length ≤ a` — the case that occurs in the\nconjugate recursion for a decreasing partition), adding it increments the\ncolumn-pair count `sumChoose2` by exactly the cell count `Σ c`.  Each of the\n`c.length` existing columns gains one cell, contributing `+ c_j` (Pascal);\nthe overhang columns start empty (`C(1,2)=0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.choose2_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.choose2_succ","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L146-L152","doc":"Pascal's rule in the `C(·,2) = ·(·-1)/2` form: `C(c+1,2) = C(c,2) + c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.length_addRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.length_addRow","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L136-L144","doc":"`addRow a c` has length `max a c.length` (the taller of new row / diagram). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sum_addRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sum_addRow","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L127-L134","doc":"Adding a length-`a` row adds exactly `a` cells: `Σ (addRow a c) = Σ c + a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sumChoose2_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sumChoose2_cons","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L122-L125","doc":"`sumChoose2` (from `S5SO3FiberAction`) on a cons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.conjugate","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L112-L118","doc":"The conjugate/transpose `λ'` of a partition given by its parts (largest\nfirst): fold the parts as successive largest rows.  For a decreasing `λ`,\n`conjugate λ` is the genuine transpose (`conjugate p.parts = p.conjParts`,\nchecked below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.addRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.addRow","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L103-L110","doc":"Add a new largest row of length `a` on top of a Young diagram recorded by its\ncolumn lengths `c`: increment the first `a` column lengths by 1, and append\nfresh length-1 columns for any overhang beyond `c.length`.  This is the\ntranspose of \"prepend a part `a`\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.aStat_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.aStat_cons","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L92-L99","doc":"**Largest-row peel.**  `n(a :: l) = n(l) + Σ l`: removing the largest (first)\nrow `a` from a decreasing partition drops the `n`-statistic by exactly the\nnumber of remaining cells `Σ l = |λ| - λ_1`.  (The head sits at index 0, so\ncontributes `0` and only shifts the remaining indices up by one.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.foldl_stepf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.foldl_stepf","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L81-L90","doc":"Closed form of the fold's `.2` component under an arbitrary start `(i, s)`:\n`s + n(λ) + i·Σλ`.  The engine behind the largest-row peel `aStat_cons`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.aStat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.aStat","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L76-L79","doc":"`n(λ) = Σ_i (i-1)·λ_i` on a partition's parts (0-indexed `Σ i·λ_i`), via the\n`(index, sum)` left fold.  Defeq to `PartitionOf5.nStat` and\n`DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.nStatList`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.stepf_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.stepf_apply","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.stepf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.stepf","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NStatConjugateGeneral.lean#L67-L72","doc":"The `(index, running-sum)` fold step defining `n(λ)`: on reading part `part`\nat current index `acc.1`, advance the index and add `acc.1 · part`.  This is\nthe same step used inline by `PartitionOf5.nStat` and\n`DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.nStatList`; naming it keeps `foldl` rewrites\nclean.  (Unfolds to their inline lambda, so `aStat` stays defeq to both.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}